  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 326 AM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nFriday and Saturday will still be hot as promised. As it stands, \nthey look to be the last days that this high pressure will still \nfully have a grip on us. The approaching low pressure center begins \nto break down the high Saturday evening with the cold front \napproaching Sunday morning. Specifics on timing are difficult, \nbut those in west-central Missouri may start to see \nprecipitation during the early morning hours Sunday. With \nnortheasterly movement initially, it will take some time for the\nfront to clear the area. Most will still see highs in the mid \nto upper 90s Sunday, though overnight lows should manage to be \nseveral degrees cooler.\n\nBy Sunday afternoon, PoPs north of I-44 are up to 30-60%. They \ncontinue to spread southeast throughout the overnight and Monday, \nthough they decrease as bit as the front becomes farther removed \nfrom the better support of the low. Those in south-central Missouri \nmay not see as much rain. From Monday onward, highs for most are \nknocked down into the 80s.\n\nThe CPC 8-14 day outlook is showing a 50-60% chance to end September \nwith above normal temperatures...but the 3-4 week outlook has equal \nchances for above and below normal temperatures. So, perhaps we can \nhold out some hope for the start of October.",
